// Formative practice quiz for project-structure. Low-stakes; answers are visible by design. First draft, not yet reviewed.
$CATEGORY: react/components-and-state/project-structure

::project-structure o1 - entry chain::After scaffolding with Vite, which file connects React to the empty root div in the page?{
~src/App.jsx#Not quite. App is the root component, but it does not locate the div. main.jsx renders it there.
=src/main.jsx#Correct. The entry script finds the root div and renders the App component into it.
~package.json#Not quite. package.json lists dependencies and scripts. It runs no page code.
~index.html, using React syntax written inside the div#Not quite. index.html only holds the empty div and loads the entry script.
}

::project-structure o1 - package.json role::A new teammate asks where the dev and build commands are defined. What do you point to?{
~src/main.jsx#Not quite. That is the entry script for the app, not a list of commands.
~index.html#Not quite. The page is what the browser loads; it defines no npm commands.
=The scripts section of package.json#Correct. npm run uses the scripts listed in package.json.
~The dist folder#Not quite. dist holds build output, not commands.
}

::project-structure o2 - named import::A file contains export function Footer. Which import is correct?{
=import \{ Footer \} from ./Footer.jsx, with quotes around the path#Correct. A named export is imported with braces and the exported name.
~import Footer from ./Footer.jsx, with quotes around the path#Not quite. No braces asks for the default export, which this file does not have.
~import \{ Bottom \} from ./Footer.jsx, with quotes around the path#Not quite. A named import must use the exported name, unless you rename it with as.
~import \{ Footer \} from Footer.jsx, with quotes around the path#Not quite. Without ./ the name is treated as a package rather than your file.
}

::project-structure o2 - default local name::A file has export default function Page. Which statement is true when importing it?{
~You must write braces around Page#Not quite. Braces ask for a named export, and this one is the default.
=You may choose any local name, with no braces#Correct. A default import binds whatever local name you write.
~The local name must be exactly Page#Not quite. Only named imports must match the exported name.
~A default export cannot be imported into another file#Not quite. Default exports exist to be imported.
}

::project-structure o3 - dev vs build::You need files to hand to a static host. Which command do you run, and where do the files appear?{
~npm run dev, and they appear in dist#Not quite. The dev server serves your source and writes no production output.
~npm run dev, and they appear in src#Not quite. src is your source. The dev server does not produce deployable files there.
~npm install, and they appear in node_modules#Not quite. That installs dependencies. It does not build your app.
=npm run build, and they appear in dist#Correct. The build writes optimized production files to dist.
}
